course: dictionary
lesson: 10377
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Treatment is one of them. The words around it are the clues, so read the whole sentence before you decide. «Children having cancer treatment must avoid germs» means medicine and care that help someone get better, because the children are ill.
explain: Treatment can also mean the way you behave towards someone. Look for words like fair or unkind near it. «Fair treatment» means treating people justly, the same as everyone else, without favourites.
explain: Treatment can also mean a way of cleaning or protecting something. «A vet gives pets flea treatment» is not about a doctor. Ask yourself: what is being treated? A person, or a thing like water, wood or a pet's bed?
fact: Treatment is a noun. It can mean care for an illness or injury, the way someone is treated, or a way of cleaning or protecting something.
fact: «Medical treatment» is care from doctors or nurses to make someone better.
fact: «Water treatment» makes water safe to drink.
fact: «Fair treatment» means treating people equally and justly.
fact: «Urgent treatment centres» deal with sprains, small cuts and minor burns.
exercise: «Children having cancer treatment must avoid germs, because the treatment makes it harder to fight infections.» What does treatment mean here? | The way a teacher behaves towards a class | *Medicine and care to make someone better | A way of cleaning water | A kind of paint for wood
exercise: «A vet gives pets flea treatment.» What kind of treatment is this? | *A way of protecting pets from fleas | A bath for a dog | Fair behaviour towards animals | Care given by a doctor to a sick pet
exercise: «Everyone in our class should get fair treatment.» What does treatment mean? | A way of cleaning water | Medicine to make someone better | *The way people behave towards each other
test: «He needed treatment at the eye hospital after the pencil hit him.» What does treatment mean? | Fair behaviour from the teacher | Playing a game | *Medical care to make him better | A way of protecting the eye from dust
test: «Water treatment makes water safe to drink.» What does water treatment do? | Stops the rain from falling | *Makes water safe to drink | Gives water to pets | Makes water hot
exam: Maya reads «The silent treatment hurt her feelings.» What does treatment mean here? | Medicine for a cold | A visit to the hospital | *The way someone is treated, here by being ignored on purpose | A cleaning product for windows
